.policy "ruff-c419-unnecessary-comprehension-in-call" revision 3
.description "Pass a generator expression to any() and all() instead of a list or set comprehension; it saves memory and lets them stop early."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff C419 (flake8-comprehensions): the builtin any or all (by name or as `builtins.any`) called with no
// keywords, whose first argument is a list or set comprehension that does not await; in the file and in string
// type definitions. The finding is at the comprehension. Ruff's preview also takes sum, min and max; this is the
// stable rule. Its fix is unsafe; none here.
//   any([x.ok for x in xs])     all({x for x in xs})     ← C419: any(x.ok for x in xs)
//   a: "any([x for x in y])" = 1                         ← C419: a string type definition is code
//   any(x.ok for x in xs)    any([await f(x) for x in xs])    sum([x for x in xs])    not reported
#include "python/python-15.rerail"
//   p15_builtin_call(c, x), p15_str_call(c, x), p15_nkw0(c), p15_first(c, a); c4_comp(e, k)

.violation C419(at: node, kind: symbol) code "C419"
    "Drop the comprehension's brackets or braces to pass a generator expression so the call can stop early; keep the comprehension only if every element must be evaluated for its side effects."
    suppress ruff "C419"
C419(e, k) :- (p15_builtin_call(c, f) ; p15_str_call(c, f)), (f = "any" ; f = "all"), p15_nkw0(c), p15_first(c, e),
    c4_comp(e, k), (k = "list" ; k = "set"), field(e, "body", b), !kind(b, "await"), !has(b, _, "await"),
    !async_for(e).
p15_name("any"). p15_name("all").
.decl async_for(e: node)  // `[x async for x in xs]`
async_for(e) :- p15_first(_, e), child(e, fc, _), kind(fc, "for_in_clause"), op(fc, "async").
